    "Continue the current loading scheme on all main lifts — the strength index improvements across every muscle group confirm the progression is working, so do not change what is not broken.",
    "Consider adding one set to biceps training next period to bring it closer in line with triceps volume, supporting more balanced arm development without meaningfully increasing total fatigue.",
    "Look for an opportunity to add one or two leg sets in the next period, as legs represent a large muscle group and modestly increasing their volume share from 22.4% could accelerate overall muscle growth.",
    "Monitor recovery closely as you carry this momentum forward — back-to-back periods of strong gains can accumulate fatigue, so pay attention to sleep quality and soreness levels as a guide for when a deload might eventually be warranted."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "All six muscle groups improved their strength index this period with gains ranging from 4 to 7 points; volume is balanced overall with mild underrepresentation of biceps and legs worth gradually addressing next period."
}
